@startuml nodemedic-arch-overview
' NodeMedic — 1000ft architecture view.
' Five boxes, six arrows. For the full detail (RBAC, tool surface,
' guardrails, FR-12 race, etc.) see nodemedic-arch.puml.

!pragma layout smetana
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam rectangleBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam packageBackgroundColor  #F5F8FF
skinparam packageBorderColor      #6B8AB8

title NodeMedic — 1000ft view\nDetect · Diagnose · Decide · Notify · Act\n(detail: nodemedic-arch.puml)

' ============================================================
' Five boxes — one per role
' ============================================================
component "**① Detect**\nNPD + custom plugins\n(NodeConditions, deterministic)" as detect

component "**② Diagnose**\nNodeMedic Agent\nClaude · multi-turn loop\nBash + NR MCP (read-only)" as diagnose

component "**③ Decide**\nNodeMedic Controller\nNHD CRD · confidence gate\n(≥0.7 conf · ≥2 sources)\n→ cordon (auto, idempotent)" as decide

component "**④ Notify**\nSlack Block Kit\n(severity-coded)" as notify

component "**⑤ Act**\nOn-Call UI\nUncordon · Drain · Clear-skipDeletion\n(human-confirmed, kube-API direct)" as act

actor "On-call engineer" as eng

' ============================================================
' Flow — six arrows, numbered for reading order
' ============================================================
detect    --> decide   : **A** NodeCondition\nflips True
decide    --> diagnose : **B** POST /diagnose\n(async)
diagnose  --> decide   : **C** status.diagnosis\non NHD CR
decide    --> notify   : **D** gate result →\nApplied · HumanInLoop · Critical
notify    --> eng      : **E** Slack page +\n"View full diagnosis" button
eng       --> act      : **F** click through\n→ review + remediate

' ============================================================
' Single side note — the safety story
' ============================================================
note bottom of diagnose
  Hallucination guardrails (layered):
   1. emit_report schema validation
   2. controller confidence gate
   3. read-only credentials
      (no mutation possible)
   4. human review on UI before
      uncordon / drain
end note

note bottom of detect
  Cloud-agnostic — same image,
  chart, runbook on EKS + Azure
  kubeadm. Demonstrated on cf1z.
end note

@enduml
